# An API token lets an agent or a script act as a user, with what that user
# may see and do, until it expires or is revoked. It is how everything but
# a browser uses the app.
#
# A token is shown once, when it is made; afterwards only a digest is kept,
# so nobody, not the app either, can show it again. A user sees and revokes
# only their own tokens, and making one needs a recent proof of who they
# are, so a token cannot be used to make another.
module Accounts::Tokens
end
